WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.670
Inside a metal kettle,

2
00:00:01.720 --> 00:00:05.110
a wire works loose and
touches the metal case.

3
00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:08.550
Now the whole case is
connected to the mains supply.

4
00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:12.230
Anyone who touches it could
get a deadly electric shock.

5
00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:14.990
But if the plug and
cable are wired properly,

6
00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:17.850
the moment the fault happens,
the kettle is made safe,

7
00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:20.090
and nobody gets hurt.

8
00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:21.430
What saves you?

9
00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:24.830
In this mission, you'll compare
direct and alternating current,

10
00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:27.280
and meet the mains
supply in your home.

11
00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:31.690
You'll find out what the live,
neutral and earth wires each do,

12
00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:33.930
and what a fuse is for.

13
00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:37.850
Your mission: find out what stops
a faulty kettle giving you a

14
00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:39.220
deadly shock.
